1
00:00:00,733 --> 00:00:01,700
<i> The search warrant is out.</i>

2
00:00:01,833 --> 00:00:03,633
<i>Let's coordinate
with the Manila peace force.</i>

3
00:00:03,767 --> 00:00:05,867
<i>To search Major Delgado's
belongings.</i>

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,033
<i>I have proof that
he didn't kill Ramon Orbos!</i>

5
00:00:08,167 --> 00:00:09,800
<i> Don't talk to anyone.</i>

6
00:00:09,933 --> 00:00:11,533
<i>That might be the reason
someone's after you.</i>

7
00:00:11,667 --> 00:00:13,767
<i>There's something you need
to know about Lisa.</i>

8
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:15,200
<i> She's in trouble too?</i>

9
00:00:15,333 --> 00:00:17,800
<i>Someone saw her while
she was torturing Ramon.</i>

10
00:00:17,933 --> 00:00:19,500
<i> It was caught on video.</i>

11
00:00:19,633 --> 00:00:23,500
<i>Is Major Delgado really
the number one suspect?</i>

12
00:00:23,633 --> 00:00:25,167
<i> Isn't it too convenient</i>

13
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:29,733
<i>that the gun used to kill Orbos
was found in his car?</i>

14
00:00:29,867 --> 00:00:31,067
<i> Come with us, Major.</i>

15
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:32,367
<i> I have evidence!</i>

16
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:34,200
<i> You can't take my dad, please!</i>

17
00:00:34,367 --> 00:00:35,700
<i>Mom, I need to go back
to the market.</i>

18
00:00:35,833 --> 00:00:37,400
<i>I think I left
the flash drive there.</i>

19
00:00:37,533 --> 00:00:40,333
<i>When I get back, I'll have the
proof that can set dad free.</i>

20
00:00:40,467 --> 00:00:43,100
<i>Parak already made sure Delgado
would end up in jail.</i>

21
00:00:43,233 --> 00:00:45,867
<i>Nothing will stand in the way
of our operation in Bolagos.</i>

22
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:46,900
<i> I was set up.</i>

23
00:00:47,033 --> 00:00:48,133
<i> That gun isn't mine.</i>

24
00:00:48,267 --> 00:00:50,167
<i> Cruz, bring him in.</i>

25
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:51,400
<i> Boss, he's here.</i>

26
00:00:51,533 --> 00:00:52,600
<i> There he is.</i>

27
00:00:52,733 --> 00:00:54,200
<i> The man of the hour.</i>

28
00:00:54,333 --> 00:00:55,767
<i> Good job, Parak.</i>

29
00:01:16,567 --> 00:01:20,000
Delgado's been a thorn
in our flesh for a long time.

30
00:01:20,133 --> 00:01:22,300
Good thing he's finally
been silenced.

31
00:01:22,433 --> 00:01:25,067
Even if he talks inside
that cell,

32
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:26,833
no one will believe him anymore.

33
00:01:26,967 --> 00:01:30,067
His name's completely ruined.

34
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:31,600
I told you.

35
00:01:31,733 --> 00:01:33,600
Just let me handle it

36
00:01:33,733 --> 00:01:35,633
and everything will fall
into place.

37
00:01:40,767 --> 00:01:44,033
<i>I was cornered,
that's why I gave the tip.</i>

38
00:01:44,667 --> 00:01:47,533
<i>I don't want my business
to be shut down!</i>

39
00:01:47,667 --> 00:01:50,200
<i>So you dropped Berdugo's
business instead?</i>

40
00:01:51,333 --> 00:01:54,033
<i>Diego, come on. I'm sorry,
it won't happen again.</i>

41
00:01:54,167 --> 00:01:56,400
<i> That's over now.</i>

42
00:01:56,533 --> 00:01:58,333
<i>Yesterday, a reporter
approached me,</i>

43
00:01:58,467 --> 00:02:01,133
<i> but I didn't say a word.</i>

44
00:02:01,267 --> 00:02:02,433
<i> I'm sorry, Diego.</i>

45
00:02:02,567 --> 00:02:05,467
<i>I'll keep quiet,
just don't kill me.</i>

46
00:02:07,133 --> 00:02:08,767
<i>I don't want you to keep quiet.</i>

47
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:10,767
<i> I want you to sing.</i>

48
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:13,433
<i> But here's what we'll do,</i>

49
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:16,200
<i>I'll dictate the lyrics to you.</i>

50
00:02:16,333 --> 00:02:17,733
<i> That's what I want you to do.</i>

51
00:02:17,867 --> 00:02:21,500
The first thing I ruined
was Delgado's name.

52
00:02:21,633 --> 00:02:25,233
So when I deliver
the final blow...

53
00:02:26,433 --> 00:02:29,100
no matter what happens,
no one will stand against me.

54
00:02:29,233 --> 00:02:32,267
But how did you manage
to get him arrested?

55
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:33,433
Simple.

56
00:02:33,567 --> 00:02:36,667
I planted a gun in his car, why?

57
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:39,433
Simple but very effective.

58
00:02:42,533 --> 00:02:44,067
That's what I like
about you, Parak.

59
00:03:00,067 --> 00:03:02,767
<i>You know, we should've
used your car instead.</i>

60
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:06,100
<i> Mine doesn't match your image.</i>

61
00:03:06,233 --> 00:03:09,367
<i>What could I do?
My car's at the shop.</i>

62
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:10,467
<i>- At the shop?
- Yes!</i>

63
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:12,467
<i> Upgrading again?</i>

64
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:14,033
<i> You're really something else.</i>

65
00:03:14,167 --> 00:03:15,667
<i> Your watch, upgraded.</i>

66
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:17,033
<i> Your clothes...</i>

67
00:03:18,267 --> 00:03:21,167
<i> even your shoes are upgraded!</i>

68
00:03:21,333 --> 00:03:23,067
<i>Who knows where those came from?</i>

69
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:24,300
<i> Hey, don't joke like that.</i>

70
00:03:24,433 --> 00:03:25,967
<i> That's not funny.</i>

71
00:03:26,100 --> 00:03:29,433
<i>What do you want me to do? I
don't have a family to spend on.</i>

72
00:03:29,567 --> 00:03:32,267
<i>Why shouldn't I treat
myself, right?</i>

73
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:34,100
<i>Oh, so that's why
you're treating me?</i>

74
00:03:34,233 --> 00:03:35,300
<i> Of course.</i>

75
00:03:35,433 --> 00:03:38,033
<i>Who knows when the next
payday's coming, right?</i>

76
00:03:38,167 --> 00:03:39,067
<i> Let's go then.</i>

77
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:41,233
<i> Okay, okay.</i>

78
00:03:41,367 --> 00:03:43,367
<i> Buddy, wait. My...</i>

79
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:45,033
<i> wallet.</i>

80
00:03:48,633 --> 00:03:53,467
<i>Hey, check the bag
if it's there.</i>

81
00:04:05,333 --> 00:04:07,333
<i>- It's not here!
- What? It's not there, Buddy?</i>

82
00:04:07,467 --> 00:04:08,833
<i> Not here.</i>

83
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:11,833
<i> Here it is!</i>

84
00:04:13,567 --> 00:04:15,033
<i> Here it is, Buddy.</i>

85
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:16,900
It's bad if this gets lost.

86
00:04:17,033 --> 00:04:18,700
We'll need this
to save us today.

87
00:04:20,333 --> 00:04:21,733
- Let's go.
- Okay.

88
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:28,167
Parak...

89
00:04:28,333 --> 00:04:29,633
are you still with us?

90
00:04:32,233 --> 00:04:33,800
What is it?

91
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,633
I was saying,

92
00:04:36,767 --> 00:04:40,833
maybe you can help Lisa
with her problem too.

93
00:04:40,967 --> 00:04:44,667
Someone saw her torturing Ramon.

94
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:46,333
There's even a video.

95
00:04:46,467 --> 00:04:48,900
It might be used against us.

96
00:04:49,033 --> 00:04:51,333
- Of course, as long as...
- I can find it on my own.

97
00:04:52,367 --> 00:04:55,867
You know, I like taking care
of my own mess.

98
00:04:56,733 --> 00:04:58,900
Are you sure you can handle it?

99
00:04:59,033 --> 00:05:02,967
This is not my first rodeo,
Matias.

100
00:05:03,133 --> 00:05:07,467
I've faced worse
than that woman.

101
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:08,800
Okay.

102
00:05:08,933 --> 00:05:11,200
I'm just here if you need me.

103
00:05:11,333 --> 00:05:13,433
Just give me the full details.

104
00:05:13,567 --> 00:05:16,433
You know, I might even be able
to find that video.

105
00:06:09,333 --> 00:06:11,533
Did you see a heart-shaped
flash drive around here?

106
00:06:11,667 --> 00:06:13,933
Maybe you saw it while sweeping.

107
00:06:14,067 --> 00:06:15,900
No, I just finished sweeping.

108
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:22,500
Miss, are you sure you didn't
see a USB shaped like a heart?

109
00:06:22,633 --> 00:06:25,467
It looks like a jewelry
or a keychain.

110
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:27,033
None.

111
00:06:28,500 --> 00:06:31,433
Please let me know
if you find it, okay?

112
00:06:32,867 --> 00:06:34,233
Thank you.

113
00:06:35,433 --> 00:06:36,933
It's not there either.

114
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:41,133
Sorry, I'm late.

115
00:06:41,300 --> 00:06:44,600
Because I checked
in Bolagos too.

116
00:06:44,733 --> 00:06:49,367
They really went through with
it, Miguel's already in jail.

117
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:52,533
We probably won't be able
to talk to him tonight.

118
00:06:52,667 --> 00:06:54,900
But I still want to go home

119
00:06:55,033 --> 00:06:57,967
so I can visit him early
tomorrow.

120
00:06:58,100 --> 00:07:00,567
Okay. All right.

121
00:07:00,700 --> 00:07:02,267
- Is this it?
- Yes, this is it.

122
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:05,033
- By the way, how's Joey?
- Thank you.

123
00:07:05,167 --> 00:07:08,133
She said she'll follow.

124
00:07:08,267 --> 00:07:10,700
Is she okay?

125
00:07:10,833 --> 00:07:12,233
Of course not.

126
00:07:14,733 --> 00:07:18,867
But she mentioned she has proof.

127
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:22,100
She says she can prove
that Miguel is innocent.

128
00:07:22,233 --> 00:07:24,867
- Wait, let me just grab my bag.
- Go ahead.

129
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:27,967
It's supposedly a video.

130
00:07:28,100 --> 00:07:30,767
But she's still looking
for the flash drive.

131
00:07:33,767 --> 00:07:36,900
<i>Maybe you could also help Lisa
with her problem.</i>

132
00:07:37,033 --> 00:07:39,233
<i>Someone saw her torturing Ramon.</i>

133
00:07:39,367 --> 00:07:40,733
<i> There's even a video.</i>

134
00:07:40,867 --> 00:07:42,933
<i> She might use it against us.</i>

135
00:07:44,567 --> 00:07:47,267
What video is that, Clarissa?

136
00:07:53,633 --> 00:07:55,033
Looks like it's not there.

137
00:07:55,167 --> 00:07:57,267
Where could it be?

138
00:08:17,467 --> 00:08:19,200
It's really not here.

139
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:21,967
I don't even know.

140
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:23,833
She didn't say.

141
00:08:23,967 --> 00:08:26,967
But she said she'll show it
once she finds it.

142
00:08:27,100 --> 00:08:28,700
Oh, okay.

143
00:08:30,133 --> 00:08:31,367
- All right, let's go.
- Let's go?

144
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:32,567
Okay, okay,
I got this, I got this.

145
00:08:32,700 --> 00:08:34,600
- Okay, thanks.
- Just this one...

146
00:08:34,733 --> 00:08:35,767
Oh, okay.

147
00:08:35,900 --> 00:08:37,667
- Is this everything?
- Yes, just this one.

148
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:40,067
- Okay.
- Thank you.

149
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:41,600
<i>Godfather, was there any report
filed at the station</i>

150
00:08:41,733 --> 00:08:43,100
<i> about a missing man?</i>

151
00:08:43,233 --> 00:08:48,433
<i>Or was a body found in Bolagos
these past few days?</i>

152
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:01,467
If you see a heart-shaped USB,

153
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:03,267
please let me know.

154
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:04,367
That's my number.

155
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:05,667
Just reach out and ask nicely.

156
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:09,267
Then the load that you'll be
using, I'll just pay for it.

157
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:11,533
We'll handle it from here,
Miss Beautiful.

158
00:09:18,300 --> 00:09:21,367
We've searched every corner
of this market.

159
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:23,467
Even the places you haven't gone
to yet, I've already been to.

160
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:25,400
But really, there's nothing.

161
00:09:25,533 --> 00:09:28,233
What if you dropped it
in your stalker's car?

162
00:09:29,233 --> 00:09:31,733
Then we definitely
won't get it back.

163
00:09:33,467 --> 00:09:36,333
What do we do now, Peter?
We don't have any evidence left.

164
00:09:38,133 --> 00:09:40,200
Joey, relax, okay?

165
00:09:40,333 --> 00:09:41,400
Just relax.

166
00:09:41,533 --> 00:09:43,467
How can I relax?

167
00:09:45,367 --> 00:09:48,100
How can I relax?
My dad needs that.

168
00:09:49,267 --> 00:09:50,767
He's in jail and
I can't do anything.

169
00:09:50,900 --> 00:09:52,600
I can't help him.

170
00:09:52,733 --> 00:09:55,600
That was so important.
And I lost it.

171
00:09:57,200 --> 00:09:59,767
Joey, it's not your fault.

172
00:09:59,900 --> 00:10:00,867
They were chasing you.

173
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,900
You didn't want
that to happen, right?

174
00:10:04,833 --> 00:10:06,767
Let's go to your dad.

175
00:10:06,900 --> 00:10:09,233
I'll go with you to Bolagos.

176
00:10:10,167 --> 00:10:11,600
Joey...

177
00:10:12,667 --> 00:10:14,767
your dad needs you.

178
00:10:14,900 --> 00:10:17,233
What dad needs is the evidence
that proves he's innocent.

179
00:10:17,367 --> 00:10:19,067
And I lost it.

180
00:10:20,767 --> 00:10:22,200
What am I supposed to do?

181
00:10:36,633 --> 00:10:37,533
We've been pleading
with the chief since last night,

182
00:10:37,667 --> 00:10:39,367
but he really wouldn't agree.

183
00:10:39,500 --> 00:10:41,267
So we just came here now, Buddy.

184
00:10:42,800 --> 00:10:44,700
Joey's on her way too.

185
00:10:44,833 --> 00:10:47,333
She and Peter are already
on the bus.

186
00:10:48,267 --> 00:10:50,567
So does that mean...

187
00:10:50,700 --> 00:10:52,533
you believe me now?

188
00:10:53,733 --> 00:10:55,900
Miguel...

189
00:10:56,033 --> 00:10:58,433
You know, Clarissa,
they set me up.

190
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:01,500
That gun they found,
it's not mine.

191
00:11:02,667 --> 00:11:04,767
And Golda?

192
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:06,467
She's my informant.

193
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:08,333
Diego knows that.

194
00:11:08,500 --> 00:11:10,533
Why were you kissing her?

195
00:11:11,433 --> 00:11:12,867
Love...

196
00:11:14,067 --> 00:11:16,200
Why can't you answer?

197
00:11:17,533 --> 00:11:19,533
Oh, maybe she just felt like it.

198
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:23,433
You gave in just
because she felt like it?

199
00:11:23,567 --> 00:11:24,633
Clarissa, talk it out camly.

200
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:25,833
Clarissa, do you even see
where I am?

201
00:11:26,933 --> 00:11:28,500
I'm in jail!

202
00:11:28,633 --> 00:11:30,833
I'm locked up for something
I didn't do!

203
00:11:31,933 --> 00:11:33,367
Clarissa, I need you.

204
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:36,467
I need your trust.

205
00:11:37,567 --> 00:11:40,267
I'm here because
we're still married.

206
00:11:41,833 --> 00:11:44,500
I won't abandon you, Miguel.

207
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:48,967
But trusting you,
I don't think I can anymore.

208
00:11:50,167 --> 00:11:51,233
You know, there were things

209
00:11:51,367 --> 00:11:54,233
I thought you'd never be
able to do to me.

210
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:57,500
But betraying me?

211
00:11:58,867 --> 00:12:01,000
You did that so easily!

212
00:12:02,400 --> 00:12:04,267
You know, honestly...

213
00:12:05,267 --> 00:12:09,567
honestly, I don't even recognize
the man I married anymore.

214
00:12:10,467 --> 00:12:12,000
If that's the case...

215
00:12:13,167 --> 00:12:15,000
then don't come back here.

216
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,133
I don't need your pity.

217
00:12:44,033 --> 00:12:45,867
For Major Delgado.

218
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:56,333
Major.

219
00:12:57,533 --> 00:12:59,467
I'm not giving you an interview.

220
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:02,800
This is off the record.

221
00:13:02,933 --> 00:13:04,967
What if I tell you...

222
00:13:05,100 --> 00:13:07,467
I'm starting to doubt
what's happening to you?

223
00:13:08,500 --> 00:13:09,867
You?

224
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,833
You believe I'm innocent?

225
00:13:13,033 --> 00:13:15,400
After that exposé you did on me?

226
00:13:16,367 --> 00:13:19,400
You can't fool me, Boss Budol.

227
00:13:30,333 --> 00:13:32,800
This is from Orbos' widow.

228
00:13:33,833 --> 00:13:35,200
She wanted me to give it to you.

229
00:13:35,333 --> 00:13:36,533
It's from the gym, right?

230
00:13:36,667 --> 00:13:37,967
Yup.

231
00:13:38,100 --> 00:13:39,567
I already went there.

232
00:13:39,700 --> 00:13:44,033
And I found a notebook
among Orbos' things.

233
00:13:56,433 --> 00:13:58,733
Hey, hey.
Don't open it yet.

234
00:14:00,333 --> 00:14:02,233
There are things written
in there...

235
00:14:03,267 --> 00:14:05,667
that I can't understand,

236
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:08,733
and I need your help
to decode them.

237
00:14:09,900 --> 00:14:11,667
I have a feeling...

238
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:14,067
the numbers written in there

239
00:14:14,200 --> 00:14:17,300
are the key to your freedom.

240
00:14:36,867 --> 00:14:38,000
- Joey!
- Sir.

241
00:14:38,133 --> 00:14:40,033
- You're visiting your father?
- Yes, Sir.

242
00:14:40,167 --> 00:14:41,733
We just came from Manila.

243
00:14:41,867 --> 00:14:43,600
Head straight
to the visiting area.

244
00:14:43,733 --> 00:14:44,900
Wait there for now.

245
00:14:45,033 --> 00:14:47,067
Andrew Dizon is still
interviewing your father.

246
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:48,967
Andrew Dizon?

247
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:50,200
Sir, why would you allow that?

248
00:14:50,333 --> 00:14:52,033
He's going to ruin
my father's life!

249
00:14:54,500 --> 00:14:56,167
Joey, wait!

250
00:15:00,233 --> 00:15:01,900
Aren't you angry at the police?

251
00:15:03,233 --> 00:15:05,033
Why are you helping me?

252
00:15:05,167 --> 00:15:07,000
What do you get out of this?

253
00:15:08,333 --> 00:15:10,267
I just want the truth out,
Major.

254
00:15:11,400 --> 00:15:13,067
You know...

255
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:17,233
I've been a victim of
covering up the truth before.

256
00:15:17,367 --> 00:15:19,367
That's why exposés
became my mission.

257
00:15:20,433 --> 00:15:22,667
And that matters more to me,

258
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:25,467
than my anger toward men
in uniform.

259
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:28,500
You just want fame.

260
00:15:29,533 --> 00:15:31,567
You want more followers.

261
00:15:32,333 --> 00:15:33,500
Okay, fine.

262
00:15:33,633 --> 00:15:35,500
It's not like I've got anything
else to do here...

263
00:15:36,767 --> 00:15:39,100
I'll read this notebook.

264
00:15:40,133 --> 00:15:41,867
How fast?

265
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,267
Dad!

266
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:45,033
Don't talk to him!

267
00:15:46,133 --> 00:15:48,000
What are you doing here?

268
00:15:48,133 --> 00:15:50,200
Are you happy about what's
happening to my father?

269
00:15:51,733 --> 00:15:55,000
If he deserves it, why not?

270
00:15:55,133 --> 00:15:56,100
You've got some nerve!

271
00:15:56,233 --> 00:15:57,100
Joey, stop.

272
00:15:58,333 --> 00:15:59,600
We're in a police station.

273
00:16:09,567 --> 00:16:11,200
Dad, what is that Andrew Dizon
telling you?

274
00:16:11,333 --> 00:16:12,733
I feel like giving him
a flying kick.

275
00:16:13,767 --> 00:16:15,800
Don't mind him.

276
00:16:15,933 --> 00:16:17,767
What matter is that you're here.

277
00:16:19,333 --> 00:16:21,967
The only person
who believes in me...

278
00:16:22,100 --> 00:16:23,200
completely.

279
00:16:29,533 --> 00:16:31,200
Dad, I'm sorry.

280
00:16:33,467 --> 00:16:36,433
I really can't find
the evidence.

281
00:16:36,567 --> 00:16:40,267
I think I lost it when my things
dropped at the market.

282
00:16:41,733 --> 00:16:42,933
What evidence is that?

283
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,000
And why are they chasing you?

284
00:16:47,400 --> 00:16:49,567
Because I saw Ramon Orbos.

285
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:52,100
A woman was torturing him,

286
00:16:52,233 --> 00:16:55,433
and there were others with her,
part of a syndicate.

287
00:16:56,433 --> 00:16:59,033
So I'm sure of it, it was them.

288
00:16:59,167 --> 00:17:01,400
They're the ones
who killed Ramon Orbos.

289
00:17:02,333 --> 00:17:04,933
That might be the reason why
they are looking for you.

290
00:17:06,633 --> 00:17:08,267
You are in danger.

291
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:11,333
And Peter might get dragged
into this too.

292
00:17:12,633 --> 00:17:14,633
Uncle, I'm okay.

293
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:18,067
The reason I'm helping Joey
is because I believe that...

294
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:19,633
you couldn't have done that.

295
00:17:20,700 --> 00:17:22,500
Dad...

296
00:17:22,633 --> 00:17:25,333
what if I give a statement too?

297
00:17:25,467 --> 00:17:26,733
I'm a witness.

298
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:29,267
Joey, they won't believe you.

299
00:17:30,367 --> 00:17:33,133
Especially since, you're
Uncle Miguel's daughter.

300
00:17:33,267 --> 00:17:35,067
That's why a video
would be better.

301
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:37,100
No, that's enough!

302
00:17:37,233 --> 00:17:38,233
Starting today,

303
00:17:38,367 --> 00:17:40,733
I'll have your Godfather Diego
to keep an on you.

304
00:17:40,867 --> 00:17:43,000
For your safety.

305
00:17:43,133 --> 00:17:44,900
And stop looking for that video.

306
00:17:46,267 --> 00:17:48,000
Dad...

307
00:17:48,167 --> 00:17:50,433
And don't you dare mention
any of this to anyone...

308
00:17:51,800 --> 00:17:54,900
not even to your Godfather Diego
or your mother.

309
00:17:55,033 --> 00:17:56,733
Dad, what about you?

310
00:17:56,867 --> 00:17:59,100
Promise me.

311
00:18:12,400 --> 00:18:14,000
But Dad, what if...

312
00:18:14,133 --> 00:18:15,233
what if the evidence
is really gone?

313
00:18:15,367 --> 00:18:17,033
How will you clear your name?

314
00:18:18,067 --> 00:18:19,333
I'll handle it.

315
00:18:20,433 --> 00:18:23,500
I'm doing something
to clear my name.

316
00:18:23,667 --> 00:18:25,300
I'm getting help from...

317
00:18:27,900 --> 00:18:29,367
from Boss Budol.

318
00:18:31,100 --> 00:18:32,767
Andrew Dizon?

319
00:18:33,800 --> 00:18:35,767
Dad, do you really trust him?

320
00:18:35,900 --> 00:18:37,600
- Joey...
- Dad, don't.

321
00:18:38,767 --> 00:18:40,767
Trust me.

322
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:42,733
I know what I'm doing,

323
00:18:42,867 --> 00:18:44,667
and I won't get caught.

324
00:18:48,067 --> 00:18:50,533
Right? What do we always say?

325
00:18:52,900 --> 00:18:54,500
Never say die.

326
00:18:56,433 --> 00:18:58,167
Never say die.

327
00:19:15,767 --> 00:19:16,733
Are you okay now?

328
00:19:18,067 --> 00:19:19,400
Are you sure?

329
00:19:28,133 --> 00:19:29,133
Joey, Joey, don't!

330
00:19:29,300 --> 00:19:31,267
We don't even have...

331
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:33,067
Hey!

332
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:35,233
Get down from there!

333
00:19:35,367 --> 00:19:36,967
Joey on duty.

334
00:19:37,100 --> 00:19:38,767
What's your deal?

335
00:19:38,900 --> 00:19:40,967
My dad said that you're going
to help him. Is that true?

336
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:44,533
Hey, what are you doing?
Let her go!

337
00:19:44,667 --> 00:19:46,500
You're really rude!

338
00:19:46,633 --> 00:19:48,333
You're really going to grab me
without my consent?

339
00:19:48,467 --> 00:19:51,433
I'm just stopping you
because you talk too much.

340
00:19:51,567 --> 00:19:53,167
So now you're denying it?

341
00:19:53,300 --> 00:19:54,300
So I was right,

342
00:19:54,433 --> 00:19:55,367
you're just stringing
my dad along,

343
00:19:55,500 --> 00:19:56,800
pretending you'll help him!

344
00:19:56,933 --> 00:19:58,833
Shut up.

345
00:19:58,967 --> 00:20:00,933
Your problem is
you talk too much.

346
00:20:01,067 --> 00:20:02,100
You're all talk.

347
00:20:02,267 --> 00:20:04,200
I see right through you,
Boss Budol.

348
00:20:04,333 --> 00:20:06,567
I don't trust you!

349
00:20:06,700 --> 00:20:09,167
I guess you really
are one sided...

350
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,567
just like your vlogs.

351
00:20:11,700 --> 00:20:12,833
Wow...

352
00:20:12,967 --> 00:20:14,133
So you do watch me.

353
00:20:14,267 --> 00:20:16,233
You're my secret fan.

354
00:20:16,367 --> 00:20:17,167
You know what?

355
00:20:17,300 --> 00:20:18,733
Word of advice.

356
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:22,100
Grow up.

357
00:20:22,233 --> 00:20:24,967
Your immaturity won't help
your father's case.

358
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:28,267
Why are you so obsessed with
giving unsolicited advices?

359
00:20:29,133 --> 00:20:31,300
I didn't ask for it, did I?

360
00:20:31,433 --> 00:20:32,400
And just so you know,

361
00:20:32,533 --> 00:20:33,900
I have evidence
that can help my dad.

362
00:20:34,033 --> 00:20:35,900
I just really need to find
that flash drive.

363
00:20:36,067 --> 00:20:37,000
Joey.

364
00:20:37,133 --> 00:20:38,967
Flash drive?

365
00:20:43,367 --> 00:20:45,267
What...

366
00:20:45,400 --> 00:20:46,333
flash drive?

367
00:20:51,133 --> 00:20:53,033
Why would I tell you?

368
00:20:53,167 --> 00:20:55,467
I don't even trust you,
remember?

369
00:20:55,600 --> 00:20:57,867
Can you just leave
my father alone?

370
00:20:58,000 --> 00:20:59,367
Do you even know that until now,
my parents still aren't okay

371
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:00,433
because of what you did?

372
00:21:00,567 --> 00:21:02,533
So can you just leave us alone?

373
00:21:05,167 --> 00:21:06,500
Joey, let's go.

374
00:21:06,633 --> 00:21:08,200
Come on, let's go.

375
00:21:13,700 --> 00:21:15,333
Clarissa...

376
00:21:17,067 --> 00:21:18,000
Stop that for now.

377
00:21:18,133 --> 00:21:21,167
Maybe it's better
if you just get some rest.

378
00:21:22,767 --> 00:21:24,100
It's better that
I'm doing something

379
00:21:24,233 --> 00:21:26,133
so I don't overthink.

380
00:21:28,267 --> 00:21:29,933
Come on, you...

381
00:21:30,067 --> 00:21:35,233
maybe you shouldn't dwell
on what Miguel told you.

382
00:21:39,733 --> 00:21:41,833
The nerve of him
to drove me away.

383
00:21:43,733 --> 00:21:45,367
I was hurt too.

384
00:21:46,400 --> 00:21:48,300
I'm the one who got cheated on

385
00:21:48,433 --> 00:21:51,500
so why does it feel like I'm the
one to blame for everything?

386
00:21:53,233 --> 00:21:55,033
That's exactly why you shouldn't
think about it too much.

387
00:21:55,167 --> 00:21:56,700
All right...

388
00:21:56,833 --> 00:22:00,033
I'll just go to him
and talk to him myself, okay?

389
00:22:01,633 --> 00:22:03,467
Thank you, Diego,
good thing you're here.

390
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:04,833
Of course.

391
00:22:04,967 --> 00:22:06,133
Wow, there are so many comments,

392
00:22:06,267 --> 00:22:07,333
so many posts,

393
00:22:07,467 --> 00:22:11,567
even videos calling you out,
Boss Idol.

394
00:22:11,700 --> 00:22:12,800
See?

395
00:22:12,933 --> 00:22:15,733
They're asking
where your commentary

396
00:22:15,900 --> 00:22:18,400
about Major Delgado's arrest.

397
00:22:18,533 --> 00:22:20,100
<i> You mean Miguel Delgado?</i>

398
00:22:20,233 --> 00:22:22,833
<i>I'm not sure
who he's referring to,</i>

399
00:22:22,967 --> 00:22:26,133
<i>but I'm sure
it's not Major Delgado.</i>

400
00:22:28,833 --> 00:22:30,533
I knew it.

401
00:22:30,667 --> 00:22:32,367
People are really
expecting something

402
00:22:32,500 --> 00:22:35,000
because of the exposé
you did on him.

403
00:22:35,133 --> 00:22:37,100
We need to ride this high,
Andrew.

404
00:22:37,233 --> 00:22:38,633
Let's release a feature ASAP.

405
00:22:38,767 --> 00:22:40,467
Kyle, call the segment
producers.

406
00:22:40,600 --> 00:22:42,667
Tell them we're putting out
a feature

407
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:45,500
with opinions
from different POVs.

408
00:22:50,500 --> 00:22:52,067
Hey, Andrew!

409
00:22:56,267 --> 00:22:56,967
Mom.

410
00:22:57,100 --> 00:22:58,467
Why are you only here now?

411
00:22:59,500 --> 00:23:01,167
We just came from dad's.

412
00:23:01,300 --> 00:23:03,667
I actually thought
I'd see you there.

413
00:23:03,800 --> 00:23:06,200
Your mom and I left early.

414
00:23:06,333 --> 00:23:08,600
Looks like she really
needs to rest.

415
00:23:08,733 --> 00:23:10,967
She said she stayed up last
night waiting for you.

416
00:23:11,100 --> 00:23:12,867
She didn't know where you went.

417
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:17,000
She said you were looking
for some evidence.

418
00:23:19,267 --> 00:23:20,767
I told you, didn't I?

419
00:23:21,867 --> 00:23:23,600
I want a different angle.

420
00:23:23,733 --> 00:23:26,133
Just give me a little time.

421
00:23:26,267 --> 00:23:27,633
I promise you,

422
00:23:27,767 --> 00:23:30,733
what we'll report
will be more explosive.

423
00:23:34,900 --> 00:23:36,267
Well, look at that.

424
00:23:36,400 --> 00:23:39,100
Is no one even
listening to me here?

425
00:23:41,500 --> 00:23:42,467
Oh!

426
00:23:42,600 --> 00:23:44,433
- So?
- Oh! Sorry, Madam.

427
00:23:44,567 --> 00:23:48,433
I was just checking
our FlipTok DMs.

428
00:23:48,567 --> 00:23:52,400
There's one here, he has
a message for Sir Andrew.

429
00:23:52,533 --> 00:23:54,433
Should we entertain this?
Take a look.

430
00:23:54,567 --> 00:23:56,567
Wait, I'll play it.

431
00:23:58,167 --> 00:24:01,300
<i>There's an important
video in it.</i>

432
00:24:02,333 --> 00:24:06,533
<i>It's about the cop
who died in Bolagos.</i>

433
00:24:07,867 --> 00:24:10,667
<i>I'm sure a lot of people
will be interested in this.</i>

434
00:24:12,133 --> 00:24:15,133
<i>But I'm offering it only to you,
Boss Idol...</i>

435
00:24:16,267 --> 00:24:20,467
<i>for the right price, of course.</i>

436
00:24:21,867 --> 00:24:23,200
<i>I have evidence
that can help my father.</i>

437
00:24:23,333 --> 00:24:25,400
<i>I just really need
to find that flash drive!</i>

438
00:24:25,533 --> 00:24:27,233
<i> Flash drive?</i>

439
00:24:28,600 --> 00:24:29,833
There, right?

440
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:30,933
What is that?

441
00:24:31,067 --> 00:24:32,167
Crazy, right?

442
00:24:32,300 --> 00:24:34,367
Who would believe that?

443
00:24:34,500 --> 00:24:37,567
Gives off scammer vibes,
doesn't it?

444
00:24:37,700 --> 00:24:38,933
Nevermind, this is a no.

445
00:24:39,067 --> 00:24:40,333
Don't.

446
00:24:44,067 --> 00:24:45,400
What is this, Joey?

447
00:24:46,567 --> 00:24:48,033
A video?

448
00:25:04,633 --> 00:25:06,067
The people looking for you
are here. Hide.

449
00:25:06,200 --> 00:25:08,567
I know who took it,
it was Panot!

450
00:25:08,700 --> 00:25:11,033
He's selling the USB that
contains the video

451
00:25:11,167 --> 00:25:12,567
of the late Officer Bolagos.

452
00:25:12,700 --> 00:25:15,100
The woman you're looking for,
Lisa, is probably headed there.

453
00:25:15,233 --> 00:25:17,433
I'll face them myself.

454
00:25:17,567 --> 00:25:18,800
The woman's already inside.

455
00:25:18,933 --> 00:25:20,933
They're buying the USB
from a group of addicts.

456
00:25:21,067 --> 00:25:22,033
Let's go!

457
00:25:22,167 --> 00:25:23,833
It's time to meet
that freaking girl

458
00:25:23,967 --> 00:25:25,267
and get that video.

459
00:25:25,400 --> 00:25:26,800
Take care of my wife
and child for now.

460
00:25:26,933 --> 00:25:27,867
I'll do everything.

461
00:25:28,000 --> 00:25:29,633
I'll find out everything,
whoever's behind this.

462
00:25:29,767 --> 00:25:31,700
I'll handle this investigation.

463
00:25:31,833 --> 00:25:34,400
Why, Miguel? Don't you trust me
anymore, Buddy?
